        "title": "Negotiation Kya Hai — Paisa Bachane Ka Sabse Bada Haathiar",
        "content": "### Negotiation Ka Simple Definition\n\nNegotiation ka matlab hai — **do log ya groups apni baat rakhte hain, aur ek aisa solution nikalte hain jo dono ke liye acceptable ho.** Yeh koi jhagda nahi hai, koi fight nahi hai — yeh ek structured conversation hai jismein dono parties apni needs aur wants openly rakhte hain, aur phir milke ek agreement tak pahunchte hain.\n\nSocho, tumhe ek used bike khareedni hai. Seller ne ₹40,000 manga. Tumhe lagta hai ₹30,000 fair price hai. Kya tum seedha ₹30,000 doge aur seller mana karega? Nahi — tum negotiate karoge. Tum poochoge, tum reasons doge, tum alternative dhundhoge. Yeh negotiation hai.\n\n**Negotiation = Communication + Information + Patience + Strategy**\n\n### Why Negotiation Is a Life Skill, Not Just a Business Skill\n\nBahut log sochte hain negotiation sirf business deals mein hoti hai. Galat! Negotiation har roz hoti hai:\n\n| Situation | Negotiation Type | Paisa Impact |\n|-----------|-----------------|--------------|\n| Auto-rider se fare | Micro-negotiation | ₹20-50 per ride |\n| College hostel fees | Fee negotiation | ₹5,000-20,000/year |\n| First job salary | Salary negotiation | ₹1-5 LPA lifetime impact |\n| Rent with landlord | Rent negotiation | ₹2,000-10,000/month |\n| Bike/Car purchase | Purchase negotiation | ₹5,000-50,000 one-time |\n| Internet bill | Bill negotiation | ₹200-500/month |\n| Freelance project | Rate negotiation | ₹5,000-50,000/project |\n\n**Key Insight:** Agar tumhe lagta hai negotiation sirf \"paise kam karne\" ke liye hai, toh socho — negotiation tumhe **better deals, better salary, better opportunities** dilati hai. Har ₹1 negotiation mein ₹1 saved ya earned hota hai. Over a lifetime, yeh lakhs mein convert hota hai.\n\n### Indian Culture and Negotiation — Hamare Desh Ki Parampara\n\nIndia mein negotiation ek culture hai. Local markets mein bargaining karna — yeh toh humari birthright hai! Sarojini Nagar mein ₹500 ki dress ₹200 mein lena, Crawford Market mein bulk mein saman khareedna, auto walon se meter pe chalne ki negotiate karna — yeh sab hum karte hain bina soche.\n\nLekin **professional settings mein negotiation** — yeh bahut kam log karte hain. India mein ek weird culture hai ki \"paise ki baat karna bura hota hai.\" especially for women. But think about it — agar tum ₹5,000 ki cheez ₹3,000 mein le sakte ho, toh yeh bura kaise hua?\n\n**Indian Market Negotiation Tips:**\n\n| Market Type | Typical Discount | Best Time to Negotiate | Tactic |\n|-------------|-----------------|----------------------|--------|\n| Street Market | 30-50% off MRP | End of day/month | Cash payment + bulk |\n| Electronics Showroom | 5-15% off MRP | Festival season, end of quarter | Competitor quote dikhao |\n| Car/Bike Dealer | 5-12% off on-road | End of financial year (March) | Multiple dealer quotes |\n| Property | 5-10% off listed rent | Off-season, long-term lease | Advance payment offer |\n| Online Marketplace | Coupon + exchange offer | Sale events | Price tracking apps use karo |\n\n**Real Indian Context:** Haryana ke ek village se Priya college aayi. Usne pehli baar city mein dekha ki log MRP pe cheezein khareedte hain. Ghar mein toh hamesha negotiate hota tha. Usne seekha ki city mein bhi negotiation hoti hai — bas alag form mein. Electronics mein exchange offer, rent mein security deposit, salary mein joining bonus — sab negotiation ke forms hain.",
        "color": "#2563eb",
        "emoji": "🤝",
        "interactiveType": "none"
