        "title": "Salary Negotiation — Pehli Job Ka Sabse Bada Decision",
        "content": "### Why Negotiate Salary — Lifetime Impact Calculator\n\nYeh sabse important section hai is module ka. Agar tum abhi college student ho ya abhi first job dhundh rahe ho, toh sunno carefully — **pehli salary negotiate karna tumhare lifetime earnings ka 20-30% impact kar sakta hai.**\n\n**Compound Effect Calculator:**\n\n| Scenario | Starting Salary | Annual Increase (8%) | 10-Year Total | 20-Year Total |\n|----------|----------------|---------------------|---------------|---------------|\n| Accepted first offer | ₹4.0 LPA | 8% annually | ₹58.3 Lakh | ₹1.62 Crore |\n| Negotiated ₹1 LPA more | ₹5.0 LPA | 8% annually | ₹72.9 Lakh | ₹2.02 Crore |\n| Negotiated ₹2 LPA more | ₹6.0 LPA | 8% annually | ₹87.4 Lakh | ₹2.42 Crore |\n\n**Difference of ₹2 LPA starting = ₹84 Lakh more over 20 years!**\n\n### When to Negotiate vs When to Accept\n\n| Situation | Negotiate? | Kyun? |\n|-----------|-----------|-------|\n| First job offer (campus placement) | Yes | Company ne budget rakha hai |\n| Pehli internship (stipend wali) | Yes (politely) | Agar tum skilled ho |\n| Dream company, fixed CTC | Carefully | Pata karo kitna ho sakta hai |\n| Startup offer (equity + cash) | Yes | Cash component negotiable hota hai |\n| Government job (fixed pay scale) | No | Pay commission ke according fixed hai |\n| Very small company, tight budget | Thoda | Benefits negotiate karo (WFH, learning) |\n| You have multiple offers | Yes | Leverage use karo |\n| Internal promotion | Yes | Tumhara track record hai, data rakho |\n\n### Research Phase: Market Salary Kaise Pata Karein\n\n**Salary Research Tools for India:**\n\n| Tool | Best For | Accuracy | Free? |\n|------|---------|----------|-------|\n| **Glassdoor** | MNCs, IT companies | High | Yes |\n| **LinkedIn Salary** | Professional roles | Medium-High | Yes |\n| **AmbitionBox** | Indian companies | High | Yes |\n| **Levels.fyi** | Tech companies | Very High | Yes |\n| **PayScale** | Global + Indian roles | Medium | Partially |\n| **Hirist** | Tech roles India | High | Yes |\n\n**How to Research:**\n\n1. LinkedIn pe search karo — \"Software Engineer at TCS\" — dekho kitne log hain\n2. Glassdoor pe company name + salary search karo\n3. AmbitionBox pe Indian companies ki salaries dekho\n4. Seniors se baat karo — LinkedIn pe message karo, coffee pe milo\n5. HR se poocho — \"What is the salary range for this position?\"\n\n**Pro Tip:** HR se jab poochna ho, toh aise bolo:\n> \"I'm very excited about this opportunity. Could you share the salary range for this role so I can make an informed decision?\"\n\n### Negotiation Scripts for Different Scenarios\n\n#### Scenario 1: First Job Offer (Campus Placement)\n\n**Situation:** Tumhe Infosys se offer aaya hai — ₹3.6 LPA CTC. Tumhe lagta hai tum ₹4.5 LPA ke layak ho.\n\n**Script:**\n\n**Tum:**\n> \"Thank you so much for the offer! I'm really excited about joining Infosys. I've done some research on the market rate for this role, and considering my skills in [specific skills] and my internship experience at [company], I was hoping we could discuss the compensation. Would ₹4.5 LPA be possible?\"\n\n**HR (likely response):**\n> \"The offer is as per our standard fresher package. We can't really negotiate for freshers.\"\n\n**Counter-response:**\n> \"I understand there's a standard range. However, I've received another offer at ₹4.2 LPA, and I'd really prefer to join Infosys. Is there any flexibility? Even ₹4 LPA would work. I'm also open to discussing other benefits like joining bonus or relocation allowance.\"\n\n**Result:** ₹20,000 more + ₹20,000 joining bonus = ₹40,000 extra. Over 5 years at Infosys, this compounds to ₹2-3 lakh more in PF, gratuity, and future negotiations.\n\n#### Scenario 2: Internship to Full-Time Conversion\n\n**Situation:** Tum 6 mahine se internship kar rahe ho. Full-time offer aaya — ₹4 LPA.\n\n**Script:**\n\n**Tum (Manager se):**\n> \"Sir, I've really enjoyed my time here. During my internship, I [specific achievement 1], [specific achievement 2], and [specific achievement 3]. Based on the value I've added and the market rate for someone with this experience, could we discuss the compensation? I was hoping for ₹4.8-5 LPA.\"",
        "color": "#2563eb",
        "emoji": "🤝",
        "interactiveType": "none"
