        "totalCardsInTopic": 3,
        "title": "Salary Negotiation — Pehli Job Ka Sabse Bada Decision (Part 2)",
        "content": "**Manager (likely response):**\n> \"You've done good work, but the budget is fixed for this level.\"\n\n**Counter-response:**\n> \"I understand. Could we perhaps discuss a 6-month review with a guaranteed raise if I meet certain targets? Or could we look at benefits — learning budget, WFH flexibility, or a signing bonus?\"\n\n#### Scenario 3: Counter Offer When You Have Another Offer\n\n**Situation:** Company A ne ₹5 LPA offer kiya. Company B ne ₹6 LPA offer kiya. Tum Company A mein jaana chahte ho.\n\n**Script:**\n\n**Tum (Company A ke HR se):**\n> \"I'm very excited about the role at Company A. I wanted to be transparent — I've received another offer at ₹6 LPA. Company A is my first choice because of [specific reasons]. Would it be possible to match or come close to ₹6 LPA? I'm flexible on the structure — maybe ₹5.5 LPA base + performance bonus?\"\n\n#### Scenario 4: Annual Performance Review Raise\n\n**Situation:** Tum 1 saal se kaam kar rahe ho. Review accha hai. Company typically deti hai 8-10% raise. Tum chahte ho 20%.\n\n**Script:**\n\n**Tum (Manager se):**\n> \"Sir, I've had a great year. Let me share some specific achievements:\n> 1. Led the project that saved ₹15 lakh annually\n> 2. Delivered 2 weeks ahead of deadline\n> 3. Mentored 2 junior team members\n> 4. Got client appreciation email\n>\n> Based on these contributions and the market rate for my role (₹8-9 LPA), I'd like to discuss a 20% raise.\"\n\n### Email Templates for Salary Negotiation\n\n#### Template 1: Initial Salary Negotiation Email\n\n```\nSubject: Regarding Compensation Discussion — [Your Name] — [Position]\n\nDear [HR Name],\n\nThank you for extending the offer for the [Position] role at [Company]. I'm genuinely \nexcited about the opportunity and the team.\n\nAfter reviewing the offer and considering my research on market rates for this role \nwith my qualifications ([specific skills/experience]), I was hoping we could discuss \nthe compensation. The current offer is ₹[X] LPA, and based on my research on \n[Glassdoor/AmbitionBox/LinkedIn], the market range for this role is ₹[Y-Z] LPA.\n\nGiven my [specific achievements/skills], I believe a compensation of ₹[Target] LPA \nwould be more aligned with the market rate. I'm also open to discussing alternative \nstructures such as:\n- Higher base with lower variable pay\n- Signing bonus to bridge the gap\n- Additional benefits (learning budget, WFH days, etc.)\n\nI'm very keen to join [Company] and contribute to the team.\n\nBest regards,\n[Your Name]\n```\n\n#### Template 2: Counter Offer Email\n\n```\nSubject: Re: Offer Discussion — [Your Name]\n\nDear [HR Name],\n\nThank you for reviewing my request. I appreciate the updated offer of ₹[New Amount] LPA.\n\nI wanted to share that I've also received an offer from [Other Company] at ₹[Amount] LPA \nfor a similar role. While [Company] remains my preferred choice due to [specific reasons], \nthe compensation difference is significant.\n\nWould it be possible to:\n1. Match or come closer to ₹[Target] LPA, OR\n2. Offer a signing bonus of ₹[Amount] to bridge the gap, OR\n3. Include a 6-month performance review with a potential raise?",
        "color": "#2563eb",
