        "title": "Negotiation Practice Scenarios — Practice Karo (Part 2)",
        "content": "**Script:**\n> \"For a professional website with [specific features], my rate is ₹15,000. This includes [details]. I can also offer a basic package at ₹10,000.\"\n\n**Expected Response:** \"Budget is only ₹10,000.\"\n\n**Counter:** \"I can do ₹10,000 for a basic version. We can add features later as budget allows.\"\n\n**Win-Win:** ₹10,000 basic + potential future work.\n\n---\n\n### Scenario 5: Loan Rate Negotiation with Bank\n\n**Situation:** Home loan at 9.2%. Competitor offers 8.5%.\n\n**Script:**\n> \"Sir, I've been your customer for 5 years with good track record. [Bank] is offering 8.5%. Can you match this?\"\n\n**Expected Response:** \"8.7% is the best we can do.\"\n\n**Counter:** \"Could you waive processing fee as well? That would make it competitive.\"\n\n**Win-Win:** 8.7% + processing fee waived.\n\n---\n\n### Scenario 6: Expense Splitting with Partner\n\n**Situation:** Combined expenses ₹40,000. You earn ₹50,000, partner earns ₹30,000.\n\n**Script:**\n> \"Let's split proportionally based on income. I'll pay 62.5% (₹25,000) and you pay 37.5% (₹15,000). This way it's fair relative to what we earn.\"\n\n**Expected Response:** \"That seems fair.\"\n\n**Win-Win:** Both contribute proportionally, no resentment.\n\n---\n\n### Scenario 7: Money Conversation with Parents\n\n**Situation:** Parents expect ₹15,000/month. You can afford ₹8,000.\n\n**Script:**\n> \"Mummy, main ₹8,000 bhej sakta/sakti hoon regularly. ₹15,000 mere budget se bahar hai. Lekin main ₹2,000 extra har doosre mahine de sakta/sakti hoon. Festivals pe bhi ₹10,000-15,000 de dunga/dungi.\"\n\n**Expected Response:** \"Theek hai, ₹8,000-9,000 average ho jaayega.\"\n\n**Win-Win:** Family gets support, you maintain savings.",
